IMPORT prelude

-- Requisition of Resources Act 1985 (Singapore) -- what happens to a person or business whose land, vehicle, goods or labour is
-- requisitioned, and what they are paid: ss 2 (when Part 3 operates), 7 (the officer must declare his office), 12 (what may be
-- requisitioned, when title passes, the vehicle licence refund), 17 (directions to work, the 7-day limit, protection from
-- dismissal), 19 (land), 20 (work on land), 21 (vehicles, vessels, aircraft), 23 (goods), 27 (services), 28 and 29 (the 4-week and
-- 8-week claim windows), 34 (appeal on law only), 38(4), (5) (returns), 39 (modifications), 41(2A), (3), (4) (service and deemed
-- knowledge), 42(2), 43 (deemed Government employee), 44(2) and 45 (offences and penalty).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RRA1985.txt. The deposit's
-- title page says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on
-- 31 December 2021"; the running footer says "Informal Consolidation - version in force from 9/3/2025", and the latest amendment
-- annotated in the text is Act 5 of 2025 (in force 9 March 2025, s 4(1), (1A)), with Act 10 of 2024 (service, offences by bodies),
-- Act 13 of 2024 (public health emergencies) and Act 30 of 2024 (platform workers, s 27) annotated.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0095 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. SCOPED to what a person meets when the powers are used: what can be taken, for how long, the duties to
-- comply, the compensation formulas, the claim deadlines, how notice reaches them, and the penalty. Not encoded: the appointment of
-- competent authorities and authorised officers (ss 4 to 6); land possession and use powers in ss 8 to 11 beyond their effect on
-- compensation; ships' space and charter-party transfer (s 15) and its compensation (s 22); undertakings' work directions (s 16);
-- hire-purchase, mortgage and third-party interests (ss 24 to 26); the constitution and procedure of Compensation Boards (ss 30 to
-- 33, 35); s 36; the manpower register (s 37); regulations on vehicle returns (s 40); ss 46, 46A (officers of bodies corporate and
-- associations), 47 and 48.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Requisition of Resources Act 1985 -- requisition and compensation`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `2 -- Part 3 operates only by order`

-- s 2(1): "Part 3 does not come into operation except at the time and for the duration and in the manner mentioned in this section or
-- section 21G of the Infectious Diseases Act 1976." (2): the Minister may by order bring Part 3 into operation for public safety,
-- defence, essential supplies and services, or exercises. (3): "An order under this section must not be in force for a period
-- exceeding 7 days from the commencement of the order unless it has been made with the approval of the President."
GIVEN `days since the order commenced` IS A NUMBER, `made with the President's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order may still be in force` IF
    `days since the order commenced` AT MOST 7 OR `made with the President's approval`

§§ `7 -- the officer must declare his office`

-- s 7(1): an authorised officer acting against any person "must on demand declare his or her office and produce" his identification
-- card. (2): "It shall not be an offence for any person to refuse to comply" with his request, demand, order or direction "if the
-- officer refuses to declare his or her office and produce his or her identification card on demand being made by that person."
GIVEN `the person demanded identification` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer declared his office and produced his card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing to comply with the officer is excused` IF
    `the person demanded identification` AND (NOT `the officer declared his office and produced his card`)

§§ `12 -- what may be requisitioned, and when title passes`

-- s 12(1): a competent authority may requisition "(a) any chattel in Singapore; and (b) any Singapore ship or aircraft or anything on
-- board ... wherever the ship or aircraft may be". (14): the powers "for the purpose of conducting exercises ... are exercisable only in
-- relation to vehicles, vessels or aircraft". (15): "chattel" includes "any substance, machine, equipment, vehicle, vessel or
-- aircraft but does not include currency, gold, securities or negotiable instruments". s 3: "vehicle" includes "a crane, excavator,
-- tractor or mobile construction plant".
DECLARE Thing IS ONE OF
    `a private car`
    `a lorry`
    `an excavator`
    `a motor launch`
    `a light aircraft`
    `a generator`
    `a stock of fuel`
    `a stock of rice`
    `cash`
    `gold bars`
    `listed shares`
    `a cheque`

GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is a chattel` IF
    CONSIDER `the thing`
    WHEN `cash` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `gold bars` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `listed shares` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a cheque` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is a vehicle, vessel or aircraft` IF
    CONSIDER `the thing`
    WHEN `a private car` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a lorry` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an excavator` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a motor launch` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a light aircraft` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The encoding asks only about chattels in Singapore; s 12(1)(b) (Singapore ships and aircraft abroad) is not modelled.
GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing, `the thing is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `only for an exercise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing may be requisitioned` IF
        `the thing is a chattel` `the thing`
    AND `the thing is in Singapore`
    AND ((NOT `only for an exercise`) OR `the thing is a vehicle, vessel or aircraft` `the thing`)

-- s 12(6): a chattel other than a vehicle, vessel or aircraft "as soon as possession thereof is taken ... vests in the Government".
-- s 12(2)(b), (3): a vehicle, vessel or aircraft vests only when the authority serves "a notice stating that the competent authority
-- has acquired it", from "the beginning of the day on which the notice is served"; until then it is only requisitioned.
GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing, `possession has been taken` IS A BOOLEAN, `a notice of acquisition has been served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing belongs to the Government` IF
    IF `the thing is a vehicle, vessel or aircraft` `the thing`
    THEN `a notice of acquisition has been served`
    ELSE `possession has been taken`

-- s 12(10): where a vehicle with a licence to keep is acquired before the licence expires, the Accountant-General "may authorise the
-- refund ... of a proportionate part of the fee paid for the licence in respect of that part of the period of its validity which
-- remains unexpired", "if a claim for the refund is made ... in writing ... not later than 3 months after the date when the vehicle was
-- acquired". The refund is discretionary ("may"); this returns the most that may be authorised. Periods are in whole months.
GIVEN `licence fee` IS A NUMBER, `months of validity` IS A NUMBER, `months unexpired` IS A NUMBER, `months until the claim` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the licence refund that may be authorised` MEANS
    IF `months until the claim` GREATER THAN 3 THEN 0
    ELSE `licence fee` TIMES `months unexpired` DIVIDED BY `months of validity`

§§ `13 and 17 -- how long, and protection from dismissal`

-- s 13: a requisitioned vehicle, vessel or aircraft may be held no longer than "the duration for which that section is in operation".
-- s 17(1): a competent authority may direct "any person" to carry out or assist in works to cope with a disaster or public health
-- emergency; (2) the driver, operator or crew of a requisitioned vehicle to render service. (3): such a direction "must not, unless a
-- proclamation of emergency is in force, require any person to perform any work for a period exceeding 7 days or exceeding the period
-- during which this section is in operation, whichever is shorter".
GIVEN `days the section is in operation` IS A NUMBER, `a proclamation of emergency is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest a work direction may require, in days` MEANS
    IF `a proclamation of emergency is in force` THEN `days the section is in operation`
    ELSE `the lesser of` 7 `days the section is in operation`

-- s 17(4): "An employer must not dismiss an employee solely or mainly by reason of any duties or service which the employee is
-- required by a competent authority to perform pursuant to this section unless the employee is employed only for an agreed definite
-- period."
GIVEN `dismissed solely or mainly for the requisitioned service` IS A BOOLEAN, `employed only for an agreed definite period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dismissal is prohibited` IF
    `dismissed solely or mainly for the requisitioned service` AND (NOT `employed only for an agreed definite period`)

§§ `19 -- compensation for land`

-- s 19(1): the aggregate of (a) the rent a tenant might reasonably pay for the period, the landlord paying property tax, repairs and
-- insurance; (b) "the cost of making good any damage", "no account being taken of fair wear and tear or damage caused by disaster or
-- war operations"; (c) expenses reasonably incurred complying with directions. Proviso (e): the damage sum must not be "greater than
-- the value of the land at the time when possession ... was taken". (2): rent accrues day to day but need not be paid "at intervals of
-- less than 3 months". The damage figure supplied is taken to exclude fair wear and tear and disaster or war damage already.
GIVEN `reasonable daily rent` IS A NUMBER, `days held` IS A NUMBER, `cost of making good damage` IS A NUMBER, `value of the land when taken` IS A NUMBER, `expenses of complying` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation for land` MEANS
        `reasonable daily rent` TIMES `days held`
    PLUS `the lesser of` `cost of making good damage` `value of the land when taken`
    PLUS `expenses of complying`

§§ `20 -- compensation for work done on land`

-- s 20(1): compensation for work on land "is payable only if the annual value of the land is diminished by reason of the doing of the
-- work". (8): "no account is to be taken of any diminution or depreciation in value ascribable only to loss of pleasure or amenity".
GIVEN `diminution of annual value` IS A NUMBER, `the loss is only of pleasure or amenity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compensation for work on land is payable` IF
    `diminution of annual value` GREATER THAN 0 AND (NOT `the loss is only of pleasure or amenity`)

§§ `21 -- compensation for a requisitioned vehicle, vessel or aircraft`

-- s 21(1): the aggregate of (a) the hire a person would reasonably pay for the period, bearing insurance, maintenance and running; (b)
-- the cost of making good damage "not resulting in a total loss", no account of fair wear and tear; (c) on a total loss, its value
-- "immediately before the occurrence of the damage which caused the loss". (3): nothing for loss or damage "arising in consequence of
-- any disaster or war operations, unless it is shown that ... the risk ... was materially increased by reason of the requisition".
-- Under (3) the hire in (a) is still payable; only (b) and (c) fall away.
GIVEN `reasonable daily hire` IS A NUMBER, `days requisitioned` IS A NUMBER, `cost of repairs` IS A NUMBER, `a total loss occurred` IS A BOOLEAN, `value before the loss` IS A NUMBER, `caused by disaster or war operations` IS A BOOLEAN, `the requisition materially increased the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation for a requisitioned vehicle` MEANS
    `reasonable daily hire` TIMES `days requisitioned`
    PLUS (IF `caused by disaster or war operations` AND (NOT `the requisition materially increased the risk`) THEN 0
          ELSE IF `a total loss occurred` THEN `value before the loss`
               ELSE `cost of repairs`)

§§ `23 -- compensation for requisitioned goods`

-- s 23(1): the price the owner "might reasonably have been expected to obtain upon a sale", no account of appreciation due to disaster
-- or war. (2): it must not exceed, for an owner who (a) "had produced the goods with a view to the sale", the cost of producing them
-- plus a reasonable profit; (b) bought them "with a view to the sale", the reasonable purchase price plus a reasonable profit; "and,
-- in assessing such compensation in any other case, no account is to be taken of any profit". (3): never more than a price or maximum
-- price "fixed by law". (5): plus expenses reasonably incurred complying with directions.
-- For an owner who neither made nor bought for sale, the encoding takes the sale price supplied as already excluding profit.
DECLARE Owner IS ONE OF
    `a producer of the goods for sale`
    `a trader who bought the goods for sale`
    `an owner holding the goods for own use`

GIVEN `the owner` IS A Owner, `reasonable sale price` IS A NUMBER, `cost or purchase price` IS A NUMBER, `reasonable profit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the price compensation before any legal maximum` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the owner`
    WHEN `an owner holding the goods for own use` THEN `reasonable sale price`
    OTHERWISE `the lesser of` `reasonable sale price` (`cost or purchase price` PLUS `reasonable profit`)

GIVEN `the owner` IS A Owner, `reasonable sale price` IS A NUMBER, `cost or purchase price` IS A NUMBER, `reasonable profit` IS A NUMBER, `a price is fixed by law` IS A BOOLEAN, `the price fixed by law` IS A NUMBER, `expenses of complying` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation for goods` MEANS
    (IF `a price is fixed by law`
     THEN `the lesser of` (`the price compensation before any legal maximum` `the owner` `reasonable sale price` `cost or purchase price` `reasonable profit`) `the price fixed by law`
     ELSE `the price compensation before any legal maximum` `the owner` `reasonable sale price` `cost or purchase price` `reasonable profit`)
    PLUS `expenses of complying`

§§ `27 -- compensation for requisitioned services`

-- s 27(2): a person (a) "employed under a contract of service" is paid "the rate of remuneration payable ... under that contract on the
-- day immediately preceding" the requisition; (b) self-employed, and (ba) a platform worker, what he "would have derived" had the
-- service not been requisitioned; (c) unemployed, "such reasonable remuneration as may be fixed by the competent authority"; (d) an
-- undertaking, reasonable remuneration fixed by the authority. (4): no compensation under (a), (b) or (ba) where the contract "would
-- have been terminated by reason of any emergency or war operations", or the self-employed person or platform worker "would not have
-- derived ... any income by reason of any disaster or war operations"; he is then paid under (c).
DECLARE Worker IS ONE OF
    `an employee`
    `a self-employed person`
    `a platform worker`
    `an unemployed person`
    `an undertaking`

GIVEN `the worker` IS A Worker, `contract rate the day before` IS A NUMBER, `earnings that would have been derived` IS A NUMBER, `rate fixed by the competent authority` IS A NUMBER, `the work or income would have been lost anyway` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the remuneration for requisitioned service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the worker`
    WHEN `an employee` THEN
        IF `the work or income would have been lost anyway` THEN `rate fixed by the competent authority` ELSE `contract rate the day before`
    WHEN `a self-employed person` THEN
        IF `the work or income would have been lost anyway` THEN `rate fixed by the competent authority` ELSE `earnings that would have been derived`
    WHEN `a platform worker` THEN
        IF `the work or income would have been lost anyway` THEN `rate fixed by the competent authority` ELSE `earnings that would have been derived`
    OTHERWISE `rate fixed by the competent authority`

-- s 27(3): for an employee the authority "may disregard any allowances, ex gratia payments or other benefits ... unless the competent
-- authority is satisfied that such allowances ... had been paid to or enjoyed by the person for a period of 6 months immediately
-- before" the requisition.
GIVEN `months the allowance was paid before the requisition` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the allowance may be disregarded` IF
    `months the allowance was paid before the requisition` LESS THAN 6

§§ `28 and 29 -- the offer, the 4-week and 8-week windows`

-- s 28(1), (2): the person who gave up the property or service receives a receipt, and at the end of the period a damage notice, each
-- stating the compensation offered. (3): the claimant "is deemed to have accepted the offer ... unless, within 4 weeks from the time
-- at which the claimant received the receipt or notice, the claimant gives notice ... that the claimant claims some specified greater
-- amount or rate". Day counts below are from receipt; day 28 is taken to be within 4 weeks.
GIVEN `days after receipt when a greater amount was claimed` IS A NUMBER, `a greater amount was claimed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offer is deemed accepted` IF
    NOT (`a greater amount was claimed` AND `days after receipt when a greater amount was claimed` AT MOST 28)

-- s 29(1): any dispute whether compensation is payable or how much "must be referred to a Compensation Board". (2): an application
-- "must not be made before the expiry of 4 weeks from the making of the claim under section 28(3) or (4) unless a notification has been
-- given to the applicant under section 28(5); and where such notification contains a further offer ... the person ... is deemed to
-- have accepted the offer unless the person makes such an application within 8 weeks from receipt of the notification".
GIVEN `days since the claim` IS A NUMBER, `the authority has replied under s 28(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an application to the Compensation Board may now be made` IF
    `days since the claim` GREATER THAN 28 OR `the authority has replied under s 28(5)`

GIVEN `days after the further offer when the application was made` IS A NUMBER, `an application was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the further offer is deemed accepted` IF
    NOT (`an application was made` AND `days after the further offer when the application was made` AT MOST 56)

§§ `34 -- the Board's decision is final, except on law`

-- s 34(1): "a decision of a Compensation Board is final and binding on the parties". (2): "An appeal lies to the General Division of
-- the High Court on any question of law arising out of a decision".
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `the Board misread section 21`
    `the Board valued the lorry too low`
    `the Board preferred the other side's valuer`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal lies to the High Court` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the Board misread section 21` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `38 -- returns from businesses`

-- s 38(1): a competent authority may require "any person carrying on any undertaking" to furnish particulars on manpower and other
-- resources. (4): "No person is bound to furnish any particulars or information other than those which are accessible to the person in
-- or derived by the person from any business, occupation or work in the conduct or supervision of which the person is engaged." (5):
-- failing to furnish is an offence, fine up to $10,000 or imprisonment up to 2 years or both.
GIVEN `a requisition was served` IS A BOOLEAN, `the information was furnished` IS A BOOLEAN, `the information is accessible from the person's own business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to make the return is an offence` IF
    `a requisition was served` AND (NOT `the information was furnished`) AND `the information is accessible from the person's own business`

§§ `39 -- modifications to vehicles, vessels and aircraft`

-- s 39(1): owners may be directed "to carry out such modifications or install any equipment ... useful for defence or public safety
-- purposes". (2): "The competent authority must pay for the cost". (3): the owner "must not be required to make any modification or
-- install any equipment which would render the owner's vehicle ... unfit for the purpose for which [it] is being used by the owner".
GIVEN `the modification would make it unfit for the owner's use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may be required to make the modification` IF
    NOT `the modification would make it unfit for the owner's use`

GIVEN `cost of the modification` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the owner pays for the modification` MEANS 0

§§ `41 -- how a notice reaches you`

-- s 41(2) lists general methods; (2A): email (2)(e) and electronic notice (2)(f) "may be effected only with the addressee's prior
-- consent". (3): broadcast, public address or siren, telephone to a household member, telephone to someone at the business, SMS, and
-- fax are available only for "a notice of requisition issued pursuant to section 12 or an order or direction issued pursuant to section
-- 16 or 17". (4): deemed knowledge -- (b) registered post "on the expiry of 48 hours from the time at which it was delivered to the post
-- office"; (ba) email, (bb) electronic notice, (c) broadcast or siren, (d) leaving at the address or the telephone methods, and (e) SMS
-- or fax: "on the expiry of 6 hours". (a) newspapers or Gazette: "by noon on the day following the date of publication" (not in hours,
-- so not in the enumeration). Subsection (4) speaks only of notices under ss 12, 16 and 17.
-- (7): once deemed to know, "ignorance of the fact that the order ... has been duly served ... is not an excuse".
DECLARE Method IS ONE OF
    `registered post`
    `email`
    `an electronic notice`
    `leaving it at the home address`
    `a radio and television broadcast`
    `a siren or public address`
    `a telephone call to a household member`
    `a text message`
    `a fax`

GIVEN `the method` IS A Method, `the addressee consented beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is a notice under section 12, 16 or 17` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the method is a valid way to serve it` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `email` THEN `the addressee consented beforehand`
    WHEN `an electronic notice` THEN `the addressee consented beforehand`
    WHEN `a radio and television broadcast` THEN `it is a notice under section 12, 16 or 17`
    WHEN `a siren or public address` THEN `it is a notice under section 12, 16 or 17`
    WHEN `a telephone call to a household member` THEN `it is a notice under section 12, 16 or 17`
    WHEN `a text message` THEN `it is a notice under section 12, 16 or 17`
    WHEN `a fax` THEN `it is a notice under section 12, 16 or 17`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the method` IS A Method
GIVETH A NUMBER
`hours until the notice is deemed known` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `registered post` THEN 48
    OTHERWISE 6

§§ `42, 43 -- deemed Government employee`

-- s 42(2): a person using a vehicle under a requisitioning order "is deemed, as respects any claim in respect of injury or damage to
-- any other person or property, to be so using the vehicle as an employee of the Government". s 43: a person carrying out work under
-- a s 17 direction "is deemed, as respects any claim in respect of death or injury sustained by the person, to be an employee of the
-- Government".
GIVEN `driving a requisitioned vehicle under the order` IS A BOOLEAN, `working under a section 17 direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `treated as a Government employee for the claim` IF
    `driving a requisitioned vehicle under the order` OR `working under a section 17 direction`

§§ `44, 45 -- offences and arrest`

-- s 45: failing to furnish a requisitioned chattel, failing to give information, false information, false answers, failing to
-- register, failing to attend, wilful obstruction, and contravening any provision, order or direction: "a fine not exceeding $10,000
-- or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or ... both". The same ceilings appear in ss 9(2), 15(1) and 38(5).
-- s 44(1): police and authorised officers may arrest without warrant; (2) a person not released must be produced before a Magistrate
-- "within 24 hours (excluding the time of any necessary journey)".
DECLARE Penalty HAS
    `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
    `maximum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
    `both may be imposed` IS A BOOLEAN

`the penalty under section 45` MEANS Penalty WITH `maximum fine` IS 10000, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS 24, `both may be imposed` IS TRUE

GIVEN `hours held excluding necessary journeys` IS A NUMBER, `produced before a Magistrate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the detention is overdue` IF
    (NOT `produced before a Magistrate`) AND `hours held excluding necessary journeys` GREATER THAN 24
